      <t:profileDesc xmlns:t="http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0">
         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>Ethiopian manuscripts often contains a collection of text around each Gospel transmitted as part of the <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1560Gospel">Four Gospels</t:ref>.
               These may include: an introductory part containing <t:ref target="#BiographyLuke">Biography</t:ref>, <t:ref target="#TituliLuke">Tituli (the number of Tituli may vary)</t:ref>, <t:ref target="#EusebianSectionsLuke">Eusebian Sections</t:ref>, the actual <t:ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2713Luke">Gospel</t:ref> (which may be preceded by <t:ref target="#LukeGospelHeadline">a headline</t:ref>), and the <t:ref target="#PostscriptLuke">Postscript</t:ref>.
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
         <t:langUsage><t:language ident="en">English</t:language><t:language ident="gez">Gǝʿǝz</t:language></t:langUsage>
